1a_math_i_calculus_horizontal_asymptote_cb9eef3f_002_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which function has no horizontal asymptote?","options":["$f(x)=\\mathrm{e}^x$","$f(x)=\\dfrac{\\sin x}{x}$","$f(x)=\\sin x$","$f(x)=\\dfrac{2x^2}{x^2+1}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4bd740683f7679f00bffb39f","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_horizontal_asymptote_cb9eef3f_010_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $L\\in\\mathbb{R}$. Which condition makes the line $y=L$ a horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$?","options":["$\\lim_{x\\to+\\infty}f(x)=L$ and $\\lim_{x\\to-\\infty}f(x)=L$","$\\lim_{x\\to+\\infty}f(x)=L$ or $\\lim_{x\\to-\\infty}f(x)=L$","$\\lim_{x\\to0}f(x)=L$","$\\lim_{x\\to L}f(x)=+\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3d84bf61292613f7365362cf","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_horizontal_asymptote_cb9eef3f_011_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Suppose $\\lim_{x\\to+\\infty}f(x)=1$ and $\\lim_{x\\to-\\infty}f(x)=-1$. Which lines are horizontal asymptotes of $y=f(x)$?","options":["Only $y=1$, since only the limit at $+\\infty$ counts","Both $y=1$ and $y=-1$","None, because the two limits differ","Only $y=0$, the average of the two limits"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"78dc8968eedd990e68b9e324","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_horizontal_asymptote_cb9eef3f_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{3x}{\\sqrt{x^2+4}}$ for $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$. Which line is a horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ as $x\\to-\\infty$?","options":["$y=3$","$y=-3$","$y=0$","None; $f(x)\\to-\\infty$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"849181a7cefccc43ae085153","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_horizontal_asymptote_cb9eef3f_topup20261028_002","difficulty":"standard","quest